From eglenn at mit.edu  Tue Jul 11 15:32:30 2017
From: eglenn at mit.edu (Ezra Haber Glenn)
Date: Tue, 11 Jul 2017 15:32:30 -0400
Subject: [acs-r] acs version 2.1.0 update
In-Reply-To: <861spm7qf3.wl-eglenn@mit.edu>
References: <861spm7qf3.wl-eglenn@mit.edu>
Message-ID: <86shi26a7l.wl-eglenn@mit.edu>


PS, two additional thoughts for current acs-package users who are
upgrading to 2.1.0:

1) When updating, try the "clean=T" option, which may be able to
   migrate your census api key:

> update.packages("acs", clean=T)

  If this fails to migrate the key, you can always try:

> api.key.migrate()

  And, if all else fails, just re-install a key with
  api.key.install().


2) After installing (and loading) the package, we *highly* recommend
installing acs variable lookup tables on your system -- these are not
migrated, and installing them greatly speeds up the package:

> acs.tables.install()?

 (And since you are *installing* the table, you only need to do this
 once --- or just once, until new acs tables come out.)

Best.
Ezra


